---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { legal } from '../../i18n/legal';
import { localizedPath } from '../../i18n/utils';

const imprintPath = localizedPath('impressum', 'en');
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy | 9592 Solutions" pageKey="datenschutz">
  <main id="main" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-20">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold text-text-primary mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-text-secondary text-sm mb-12">Last updated: May 2026</p>

    <div class="space-y-10 leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">1. Controller</h2>
        <p>
          The controller responsible for data processing on this website is:
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-primary mt-3">
          <span lang="de">{legal.legalName}</span><br />
          {legal.street}<br />
          {legal.postalCode} {legal.city}<br />
          Germany
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Managing director: {legal.managingDirector}<br />
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`} class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors">{legal.email}</a>
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm mt-3">
          Further mandatory details are in the
          <a href={imprintPath} class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors">imprint</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">2. Data processing when visiting the website</h2>
        <p>
          When you access this website, the hosting provider automatically records information in server log
          files that your browser transmits. This usually includes your IP address, the date and time of
          access, the page requested, and your browser type and operating system. This data serves the secure
          and stable operation of the website and is not combined with other data sources. The legal basis is
          Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in secure operation). The log data is retained only as long
          as it is needed for these purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">3. Hosting and content delivery network</h2>
        <p>
          This website is hosted by Vercel Inc. (340 S Lemon Ave #4133, Walnut, CA 91789, USA). Delivery and
          protection additionally rely on the content delivery and proxy service of Cloudflare, Inc. (101
          Townsend St, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). Both providers process the technically required
          connection data, in particular the IP address, on our behalf as processors. This can involve a
          transfer to the USA. Both providers are certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, which
          ensures an adequate level of data protection for this. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">4. Cookies and § 25 TDDDG</h2>
        <p>
          This website uses no non-essential cookies and no tracking. No information is stored on or read from
          your device for advertising or analytics purposes that would require consent under § 25 TDDDG. For
          this reason there is no cookie banner on this website.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">5. Reach measurement</h2>
        <p>
          For reach measurement we use Vercel Web Analytics, a service of our hosting provider Vercel.
          Collection is cookieless: no cookies are set and no cross-device identifiers are formed. Accesses
          are turned into aggregated, anonymous statistics, for example on pages visited and the approximate
          region of origin, which do not allow conclusions about individual people. The legal basis is
          Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in data-minimising reach measurement).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">6. Contact and form</h2>
        <p>
          When you contact us through the contact form or by email, we process the data you provide, in
          particular your email address and the content of your message, in order to answer your enquiry. The
          form submission is handled technically by the service Web3Forms (web3forms.com), which processes the
          data on our behalf. The provider stores form submissions for about 30 days. The legal basis is
          Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (pre-contractual measures) and Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in answering
          enquiries).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-sm text-text-secondary mb-3 uppercase tracking-wider">7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Within the limits of the law you have the right to access the data stored about you (Art. 15 GDPR),
          and to rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction of processing (Art. 18), and data
          portability (Art. 20). You have a right to object to processing based on a legitimate interest
          (Art. 21 GDPR). Where processing is based on consent, you can withdraw it at any time with effect for
          the future. To exercise your rights, an informal message to
          <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`} class="text-accent hover:text-accent-hover underline underline-offset-2 transition-colors">{legal.email}</a>
          is enough. Independently of this, you have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection
          supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR).
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
